  <page_number>115</page_number>
  <running_head>DECLINATIONE.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p cont="true"><i>colúi Leggerà</i> ille leget.</p>
    <p><i>Nói Leggerémo</i> Nos legemus.</p>
    <p><i>vói Leggeréte</i> vos legetis.</p>
    <p><i>coloro Leggeránno</i> illi legent.</p>
    <head level="2">Imperat. mod. temp. præf.</head>
    <p><i>Léggitu</i> lege tu.</p>
    <p><i>Légga colúi</i> legat ille.</p>
    <p><i>Leggiámo nói</i> Legamus nos.</p>
    <p><i>Leggéte vói</i> legite vos.</p>
    <p><i>Léggano coloro</i> legant illi.</p>
    <head level="2">Futurum.</head>
    <p><i>Leggeráitu</i> legito tu.</p>
    <p><i>Leggerá colúi</i> legito ille.</p>
    <p><i>Leggerémo nói</i> Legamus nos.</p>
    <p><i>Leggeréte vói</i> legitote vos.</p>
    <p><i>Leggeránno coloro</i> legunto illi.</p>
    <head level="2">Opt. mod. temp. præf. &amp; Futur.</head>
    <p><i>O Dio vógliα, &amp;c. che</i></p>
    <p><i>lo Légga</i> vtinam Ego legam.</p>
    <p><i>tu Légga</i> tu legas.</p>
    <p><i>colúi Légga</i> ille legat.</p>
    <p><i>Nói Leggiámo</i> Nos legamus.</p>
    <p><i>vói Leggiáte</i> vos legatis.</p>
    <p><i>coloro Léggano</i> illi legant.</p>
    <p type="foot"><i>h. ii.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Several Italian forms are set in a more ornamental italic with swash letters and are only approximately legible. The "h. ii." mark is a signature at the foot. Some translation words such as "ille" and "vtinam" may carry minor type damage.</notes>
